      "section": "Misincorporation profile",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "The classic aDNA deamination signature: C>T rises toward the 5' read end and G>A rises toward the 3' end, both starting near 0.3 at position 1 and decaying to background within about 10 bp. Every other substitution class sits flat near background throughout, which is what the highlighted lines are picked out against. Which ends to show, how far to draw, and which substitutions to highlight all live in the Settings \u2699 popover.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
